WEBVTT

02:42.539 --> 02:43.374
Mama!

06:10.246 --> 06:11.281
Mm-mm.

07:24.921 --> 07:26.690
- Pepperoni pizza?
- Oh.

07:27.991 --> 07:29.660
You have got this
all wrapped up.

07:29.793 --> 07:31.194
Can we get pizza tonight?

07:31.327 --> 07:32.462
Not tonight, buddy.

07:32.596 --> 07:33.564
You don't even like pizza.

07:33.697 --> 07:35.498
No, I don't like cheese.

07:35.866 --> 07:38.068
Pizza's not pizza
without cheese.

07:38.569 --> 07:40.303
She's got a point.

07:40.436 --> 07:41.638
...large scale
efforts are being made...

07:41.772 --> 07:43.840
- Dad, come on. Another.
- Yeah, uh...

07:44.107 --> 07:45.942
Okay. Let's do...

07:46.076 --> 07:47.143
...our reporter
on the ground outside Cairo

07:47.277 --> 07:49.345
is Charlie Cannon.

07:50.013 --> 07:51.481
Critics suggest that

07:51.615 --> 07:53.049
three years of
almost continuous drought

07:53.183 --> 07:55.118
has forced local farmers
to find new

07:55.251 --> 07:56.352
and increasingly desperate
measures

07:56.486 --> 07:57.487
to make money.

07:58.088 --> 07:59.522
- But government ministers...
- Dad?

07:59.656 --> 08:01.157
- ...are on the defensive...
- Just a minute.

08:01.291 --> 08:02.993
...as they roll out
new major schemes

08:03.126 --> 08:05.295
in water management
and irrigation in desert areas.

08:06.096 --> 08:07.530
What is that, Seb?
What are you doing?

08:07.664 --> 08:09.232
An impression of you?

08:09.365 --> 08:11.067
Oh, that's an impression of me?
With the hands thing?

08:11.201 --> 08:12.603
Yeah.

08:12.869 --> 08:14.537
Unlike the swath of looting
that took place

08:14.671 --> 08:17.140
during the Arab Spring of 2011,

08:17.273 --> 08:18.775
the Egyptian authorities
are unsure

08:18.909 --> 08:20.410
what has caused
the current uptick

08:20.543 --> 08:21.978
- in unauthorized digs.
- Hey!

08:22.112 --> 08:23.279
- With the smuggling...
- Katie.

08:23.413 --> 08:24.247
of ancient arti--

08:25.015 --> 08:27.417
We need to practice this more,
or I'll fail it.

08:30.053 --> 08:30.754
Okay.

08:34.925 --> 08:35.926
Um...

08:40.063 --> 08:44.134
Babe, do I use my hands too much
when I'm on TV?

08:44.267 --> 08:45.802
Um...

08:46.369 --> 08:47.771
Isn't it one of your tics?

08:47.904 --> 08:48.872
My tics?

08:49.005 --> 08:50.373
Like trademarks.

08:50.506 --> 08:52.042
Like, you know,
"Good night and good luck."

08:52.175 --> 08:54.410
- Or "This is the way it is."
- Those are catchphrases.

08:54.544 --> 08:59.382
I mean, do I do too much
of this shit with my hands?

08:59.515 --> 09:02.218
'Cause that could be potentially
very annoying for my viewers.

09:02.352 --> 09:04.087
You know
what is really annoying?

09:04.220 --> 09:07.624
That you are doing it in my
peripheral vision, so stop it.

09:07.758 --> 09:08.725
Oh, yeah?

09:08.859 --> 09:10.426
- It's annoying...
- Yeah.

09:10.560 --> 09:11.361
- ...in your peripheral vision?
- It's very annoying.

09:11.494 --> 09:12.729
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

09:12.863 --> 09:13.596
What about this?
Is this annoying?

09:13.730 --> 09:14.497
Is this annoying?

09:14.631 --> 09:16.900
Stop it.

09:17.367 --> 09:20.170
What about her?
Is she gonna be annoying?

09:20.737 --> 09:23.974
She's gonna be really annoying,
just like her dad.

09:24.107 --> 09:25.608
- Hmm.
-  Seb,

09:25.742 --> 09:27.310
- why did you do that?
-  I'm sorry--

09:27.443 --> 09:29.012
- Get off! Get off me!
- You always mess with my stuff!

09:29.145 --> 09:31.181
- Katie, stop! Stop it.
- That's enough.

09:31.314 --> 09:33.116
- That's enough. Come on. Up.
- No, no, no. Stop it.

09:33.249 --> 09:34.617
- Come here.
- What happened?

09:34.751 --> 09:36.653
He threw Veronica off the roof.

09:37.921 --> 09:40.190
Not gonna lie. I did do it.

09:45.495 --> 09:46.863
Oh, Seb.

09:46.997 --> 09:48.598
I was testing my new parachute.

09:48.732 --> 09:50.266
But why do you
always touch my stuff?

09:50.400 --> 09:51.601
- I never touch yours!
- I just wanted to use it.

09:53.436 --> 09:56.039
I will do murders to the guilty
and the innocent, okay?

09:57.941 --> 10:00.677
Gotta go. Come on, kisses.

10:01.577 --> 10:02.345
Mm?

10:04.447 --> 10:05.849
Who do you love most, Mom?

10:05.982 --> 10:08.118
Um...
I'll tell you after my shift.

10:10.687 --> 10:11.755
Okay.

10:13.089 --> 10:14.825
I know it's not perfect.

10:14.958 --> 10:16.459
What have you done to her?

10:16.592 --> 10:18.795
But when we get back
to Albuquerque next week,

10:18.929 --> 10:20.296
we'll bring her straight
to the doll hospital

10:20.430 --> 10:21.932
for a proper fix-up.

10:22.065 --> 10:23.533
You said we were gonna live
in New York next,

10:23.666 --> 10:24.868
not Grandma's again.

10:25.001 --> 10:26.402
Wherever we go next,

10:26.536 --> 10:28.772
I hope you stay here
on your own.

10:28.905 --> 10:30.006
Hey, that's not cool.

10:30.140 --> 10:32.242
No! You didn't even yell at him.

10:33.676 --> 10:35.445
Butterfly. Come on.

10:35.578 --> 10:38.348
Don't call me Butterfly.
I hate you both right now.

10:44.187 --> 10:45.889
I won't test the parachute
on the new baby

10:46.022 --> 10:47.423
when it comes out of Mom.

10:48.825 --> 10:50.193
Thanks, buddy.

11:17.888 --> 11:19.555
Bob. Hi, how are you?

11:19.689 --> 11:21.391
Charlie Cannon.

11:21.524 --> 11:23.059
What time is it all the way
over there in Cairo?

11:23.626 --> 11:24.861
Uh...

11:25.195 --> 11:27.097
Minutes after three
in the afternoon.

11:27.230 --> 11:30.066
Just after 8 a.m.
in New York City.

11:30.466 --> 11:32.202
Let me ask you a question,
Charlie.

11:32.335 --> 11:33.904
Do you want that
breakfast news gig?

11:37.707 --> 11:38.741
Hello, there.

11:46.682 --> 11:47.851
Layla?

11:48.318 --> 11:50.153
I'm Layla's mother.

11:50.921 --> 11:54.390
Or mom.
You would say "mom", right?

11:55.691 --> 11:57.060
Where's Layla today?

11:58.094 --> 11:59.729
She has a sick tummy.

12:00.030 --> 12:03.266
But she didn't want you to worry
when she didn't show up to play.

12:03.599 --> 12:05.435
She loves being your friend.

12:08.704 --> 12:10.773
Did she tell you
anything about me?

12:12.275 --> 12:14.610
Well,
she said you're a magician.

12:14.978 --> 12:15.846
That's right.

12:17.547 --> 12:19.082
Would you like to see a trick?

12:19.850 --> 12:21.151
- Hey.
-  Hey,

12:21.284 --> 12:22.452
I'm just about to start
my rounds.

12:22.585 --> 12:24.220
Yeah, quick one. Um...

12:25.021 --> 12:26.456
How do you feel
about our new baby

12:26.589 --> 12:28.191
growing up a Yankees fan?

12:29.259 --> 12:30.760
No fucking way.

12:30.894 --> 12:32.395
Yes fucking way.

12:32.528 --> 12:33.796
You got the job?

12:33.930 --> 12:35.832
Yep. They just called.

12:36.099 --> 12:37.600
Oh, my God.

12:37.733 --> 12:39.735
I'm trying to be quiet
'cause I haven't told the kids.

12:39.870 --> 12:41.004
I knew you'd get it. I knew it.

12:41.137 --> 12:43.273
I told you. I told you!

12:43.406 --> 12:45.942
And you didn't believe me.
Idiot!

12:46.076 --> 12:48.444
Oh, my God.
When do they want you to start?

12:48.578 --> 12:50.246
Jesus,
there's so much to organize.

12:59.923 --> 13:01.824
Ta-da!

13:01.958 --> 13:03.793
Well, Mama's not
gonna be happy we're not

13:03.927 --> 13:05.128
moving back in with her.

13:05.261 --> 13:06.262
- I'm gonna have to...
- Babe.

13:06.396 --> 13:07.630
...break it gently to her.

13:07.763 --> 13:09.232
Have you been
giving Katie candy?

13:10.300 --> 13:12.135
Like, a lot of candy?

13:12.268 --> 13:13.703
No. What candy?

13:14.871 --> 13:16.039
Ah!

13:17.040 --> 13:18.308
Your favorite.

13:20.510 --> 13:22.745
Ah? Hah. Hm.

13:28.484 --> 13:31.421
I should go now before my dad
wonders where I am.

13:31.554 --> 13:32.188
Wait.

13:34.124 --> 13:35.791
I have one more treat for you.

13:36.192 --> 13:38.228
I grew it in my own garden.

13:38.361 --> 13:41.097
It tastes sweeter
than any candy.

13:51.841 --> 13:53.676
Where did Katie get these?

13:54.310 --> 13:56.179
She only shared with me
if I promised not to tell you.

13:56.412 --> 13:57.847
Tell me what?

13:58.381 --> 14:00.816
About her friend who gives them
to her at the end of the garden.

14:06.022 --> 14:08.191
I hope you can forgive me,
Katie.

14:10.927 --> 14:11.894
For what?

14:12.162 --> 14:13.829
My final magic trick.

14:37.988 --> 14:38.888
Katie?

14:52.435 --> 14:53.403
Katie?

15:04.880 --> 15:05.748
Katie?

15:21.831 --> 15:22.632
Katie?

15:29.172 --> 15:29.872
Katie?

15:36.146 --> 15:36.946
Katie?

15:38.448 --> 15:39.615
Hey,
have you seen a little girl?

15:56.432 --> 15:57.367
Hey!

15:58.768 --> 15:59.802
Hey!

16:04.174 --> 16:04.874
Katie?

16:10.513 --> 16:11.347
Katie?

16:12.815 --> 16:14.084
Katie!

16:27.029 --> 16:28.398
Katie!

16:48.251 --> 16:49.585
Katie!

17:17.513 --> 17:19.215
Katie!

17:22.318 --> 17:23.386
Katie!

17:27.957 --> 17:30.326
Katie!

18:41.163 --> 18:43.533
This is her.
This is just from a week ago.

18:54.176 --> 18:55.010
Are you on vacation?

18:55.144 --> 18:56.379
No, no. We live here.

18:56.512 --> 18:57.513
We've been living here
for five months.

18:57.647 --> 18:58.848
He's a TV news correspondent.

19:08.824 --> 19:10.860
When was the last
time you saw Katie?

19:10.993 --> 19:12.795
11 a.m. Um...

19:13.963 --> 19:15.331
And then I went to work,

19:15.465 --> 19:17.333
and-- and you were
at home with the kids.

19:17.833 --> 19:18.734
And that's it.

19:20.636 --> 19:21.871
Mr. Cannon.

19:24.940 --> 19:26.409
About 3:00 p.m.

19:29.712 --> 19:31.213
Wait, I have these.

19:31.647 --> 19:34.216
Somebody, whoever took her,
was giving these to her.

19:48.898 --> 19:50.266
What is he saying?

19:50.766 --> 19:51.634
What is he saying?

19:57.740 --> 19:59.275
Hey.

19:59.409 --> 20:00.943
You think I don't know
what you're talking about?

20:01.511 --> 20:03.279
You think we did this?

20:03.546 --> 20:05.415
You think we did something
to our own daughter?

20:05.548 --> 20:06.882
What the fuck is your problem?

20:07.216 --> 20:09.218
Are you gonna fucking help us?

20:09.352 --> 20:10.953
Send someone out there
to find her!

20:11.220 --> 20:12.555
Somebody took our child!

20:21.030 --> 20:22.398
Breaking story
at the top of the hour

20:22.532 --> 20:24.800
here at ABQ News 82.

20:25.768 --> 20:28.571
Traffic delays on the 25
just south of Albuquerque

20:28.838 --> 20:30.906
after a large desert tortoise

20:31.040 --> 20:33.108
was spotted
trying to cross the highway.

21:41.744 --> 21:42.512
Mom?

21:45.014 --> 21:45.815
Hey.

21:46.849 --> 21:48.117
Can I use your computer?

21:49.552 --> 21:50.486
What for?

21:51.286 --> 21:52.354
Printing stuff.

21:53.523 --> 21:54.323
What stuff?

21:54.790 --> 21:55.925
Stuff I want to print.

21:56.859 --> 21:58.794
Okay. Come on, let's go.

22:21.183 --> 22:22.452
I hear you, Charlie.

22:22.585 --> 22:23.285
Dad!

22:23.419 --> 22:24.720
Hey.

22:24.854 --> 22:26.188
My last baby tooth
is finally loose.

22:26.321 --> 22:27.723
Oh, let me see.

22:28.057 --> 22:29.324
You want me to pull it out
with the pliers?

22:29.559 --> 22:30.325
- No.
- You sure?

22:37.667 --> 22:38.634
- Amen.
- Amen.

22:40.369 --> 22:41.937
Sorry, guys.

22:42.071 --> 22:44.507
Traffic was backed up
on the 25 because of a tortoise.

22:44.640 --> 22:46.041
What kind of tortoise?

22:46.175 --> 22:47.677
A truck-sized tortoise.

22:47.810 --> 22:48.878
Truck-sized tortoise?

22:49.178 --> 22:50.179
How was your day?

22:50.312 --> 22:51.547
It was good.

22:51.681 --> 22:53.315
I changed 13 catheters
in an hour.

22:53.449 --> 22:54.450
Nice work, babe.

22:54.584 --> 22:55.951
Are they the poo or pee ones?

22:56.085 --> 22:57.720
I got a call to say
I've been nominated

22:57.853 --> 22:59.254
as vice chair of my bridge club.

22:59.388 --> 23:01.256
No phone at the dinner table.

23:01.390 --> 23:02.391
I wanna show you something.

23:03.158 --> 23:04.059
What is it?

23:04.193 --> 23:05.628
It's the information about

23:05.761 --> 23:08.464
the school trip
to Europe in the spring.

23:10.633 --> 23:11.767
Why are you showing it to me?

23:12.034 --> 23:13.268
It's only six months away,

23:13.402 --> 23:14.770
and I wanted you to know
about it.

23:14.904 --> 23:16.371
You think my tooth
will come out tonight?

23:18.240 --> 23:19.241
You know,

23:19.374 --> 23:20.643
you don't need to go on this.

23:20.776 --> 23:22.745
I know I don't need to,
but I want to.

23:23.112 --> 23:24.980
Well, that's not possible.

23:26.115 --> 23:26.949
Why not?

23:27.082 --> 23:28.417
Because it's not.

23:28.784 --> 23:30.385
When's the last time
we went on a family vacation?

23:30.520 --> 23:32.121
Okay, we'll talk about this
another time. Okay?

23:32.254 --> 23:34.456
No, we won't. We never do.

23:34.590 --> 23:36.559
Don't talk back to your mom, okay?

23:37.192 --> 23:38.828
You're just scared something's
going to happen to me,

23:38.961 --> 23:40.095
but I'm not Katie, Mom.

23:41.564 --> 23:42.865
Watch it, Seb.

23:54.009 --> 23:55.645
Have I ever been on vacation?

26:09.178 --> 26:09.812
Hmm.

26:25.961 --> 26:26.896
Uh-uh.

28:21.944 --> 28:24.679
♪ Blinded by the light ♪

28:25.414 --> 28:28.583
♪ Revved up like a deuce
Another runner in the night ♪

28:31.020 --> 28:33.222
Frog. Definitely a frog.

28:33.355 --> 28:35.590
That kid's a freaking toad.

28:35.724 --> 28:36.959
How about my teacher?

28:37.426 --> 28:38.660
- Rat.
- Eh, rat.

28:38.794 --> 28:40.329
I think she looks
kind of froggy.

28:40.462 --> 28:41.663
Nah, we've been calling her
rat-face

28:41.797 --> 28:43.198
behind her back in class.

28:43.332 --> 28:45.267
- Nice.
- Okay, okay, I have a good one.

28:45.400 --> 28:48.871
- Taylor Swift.
- No bueno, Seb! She's an angel.

28:49.338 --> 28:50.639
Can't argue with that,
Sebastian.

28:50.772 --> 28:52.474
Isn't the game called,
"Rat or Frog?"

28:52.607 --> 28:53.809
"Rat, Frog, or Angel"

28:53.943 --> 28:54.977
- if it's Tay.
- Okay.

28:56.879 --> 28:58.948
- I think I'm a total frog, man.
- Yeah.

28:59.514 --> 29:00.715
- Right?
- Yeah.

29:01.183 --> 29:03.218
What about you, sweetheart?

29:03.352 --> 29:04.553
Oh, yeah?

29:07.957 --> 29:09.358
Can I get two slices today?

29:09.491 --> 29:10.792
- No.
- Of course, honey.

29:10.926 --> 29:13.662
No. You never ever finish two.
Never.

29:13.795 --> 29:15.497
- It's two slices of pizza, babe.
- No.

29:15.630 --> 29:16.932
You know?

29:19.634 --> 29:20.936
Hello?

29:21.603 --> 29:23.438
Hello.
Is this Mr. Charlie Cannon?

29:23.572 --> 29:25.440
Sorry, buddy. I'm not buying
what you're selling.

29:25.841 --> 29:27.209
No, no, no.

29:27.342 --> 29:29.744
Mr. Cannon,
my name is Bryce Vogel.

29:29.879 --> 29:32.747
I'm Deputy Chief of Mission
at the US Embassy in Cairo.

29:35.250 --> 29:36.751
Uh, just a sec.

29:37.652 --> 29:39.855
Kids, stay in the car.

29:45.060 --> 29:46.761
Hello, Mr. Cannon?
Are you there?

29:46.896 --> 29:48.463
Uh, yeah, yeah, I'm here.

29:48.597 --> 29:50.032
Is your wife with you, sir?

29:51.133 --> 29:52.634
Do you have new information?

29:52.767 --> 29:54.103
Yes, I do, ma'am.

29:55.104 --> 29:57.339
Your daughter Katie
has been found.

29:59.208 --> 30:00.709
She's alive.

30:04.947 --> 30:06.115
What?

30:32.474 --> 30:34.643
It's very important
you fully prepare yourselves

30:34.776 --> 30:36.045
for what you are about to see.

30:38.547 --> 30:42.384
Katie has suffered
extensive dermal trauma.

30:42.517 --> 30:45.520
Likely from a lack of light,
and extreme malnutrition.

30:46.421 --> 30:49.024
She's locked
in a deep catatonic state,

30:49.158 --> 30:52.827
which is causing her to make
erratic and extreme movements.

30:52.962 --> 30:54.729
Repeating abrupt noises.

30:54.863 --> 30:56.031
Strange physical tics.

30:57.866 --> 30:59.734
We have her
under heavy sedation.

31:00.302 --> 31:01.436
It helps.

31:02.371 --> 31:05.607
But her levels of distress
continue to manifest.

31:07.409 --> 31:10.179
So, you need to be gentle
and calm with her.

31:10.912 --> 31:14.049
No sudden moves. No loud noises.

31:14.716 --> 31:16.385
The Egyptian authorities
will keep her discovery

31:16.518 --> 31:19.354
out of the press
to give you and your family

31:19.488 --> 31:22.557
ample time to adjust
to your new situation.

31:25.727 --> 31:26.795
Okay to go?

32:28.590 --> 32:29.458
Hey.

32:30.592 --> 32:32.627
Hey, Butterfly.

32:32.761 --> 32:33.862
It's Mom and Dad.

32:34.963 --> 32:36.498
Yeah, yeah.

32:37.399 --> 32:39.000
Yeah, we are here.

32:40.602 --> 32:41.503
We're here.

32:47.276 --> 32:48.843
The scratches?

32:48.977 --> 32:50.745
Self-inflicted.

32:50.879 --> 32:53.115
When we admitted her,
she was clawing at her skin.

33:07.829 --> 33:10.499
Her heart sounds so strong.
So, so strong.

33:11.700 --> 33:13.535
Her vitals are all perfect.

33:13.802 --> 33:15.370
Even under testing,

33:15.504 --> 33:18.039
we haven't observed
her pulse rate rise above 85.

33:18.640 --> 33:20.342
Physically she's strong.

33:20.809 --> 33:22.811
The comfort of home
will be the best medicine

33:22.944 --> 33:25.414
to help return her
from this locked-in state.

33:31.320 --> 33:32.254
Katie.

33:53.375 --> 33:55.009
Katie. It's okay.

34:25.540 --> 34:26.608
What is this?

34:27.242 --> 34:28.843
It's a basalt sarcophagus.

34:28.977 --> 34:31.413
Between two
and three thousand years old.

34:32.046 --> 34:33.915
Katie was being transported
inside it

34:34.048 --> 34:35.584
when the plane crashed.

34:36.451 --> 34:37.986
What the fuck
was our daughter doing

34:38.119 --> 34:40.622
in a 3,000-year-old sarcophagus?

34:41.523 --> 34:43.758
If you want to smuggle something
or even someone

34:43.892 --> 34:45.560
in this country
and avoid detection,

34:45.694 --> 34:48.096
the best place
is inside our history.

34:48.563 --> 34:51.566
Blind eyes are turned to
the illegal trade of artifacts.

34:52.167 --> 34:55.204
It's the perfect
human trafficking cover.

34:56.238 --> 34:58.273
I think we should get back
upstairs to her.

34:58.740 --> 34:59.841
I remember you.

35:01.476 --> 35:04.078
You were there the day
she got kidnapped.

35:04.946 --> 35:07.949
You had a working theory
then too, didn't you?

35:08.817 --> 35:10.685
You thought
I did something to her.

35:11.620 --> 35:13.855
That was
my senior officer's opinion.

35:14.289 --> 35:15.924
Charlie, let's go back upstairs.

35:16.891 --> 35:19.261
And where's his expert opinion
tonight?

